% ============================================================================
% rainforest-layer.query.adj — a worked recall over the biology rainforest
% layer library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what's the canopy
% layer?": it states no biology fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `rainforest_layer` rows and returns the description atom + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The last query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% description, recall the layer). A word that is not one of the four layers
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents a description.
% ============================================================================

import "rainforest-layer.adj"

? rainforest_layer(emergent, $D)                            % expect tallest_trees_dominate_skyline
? rainforest_layer(canopy, $D)                               % expect deep_treetop_vegetation_layer
? rainforest_layer($L, tallest_trees_dominate_skyline)        % expect emergent — the reverse recall
? rainforest_layer(soil_layer, $D)                            % expect abstain — not one of the four layers
